{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1726 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), merged to gerrit/main as 2b136e74e7.\n\nAll four levers doubled: bridge backstop */20 -> uniform 40 min (three cron entries over a 2-hour cycle, with a test that derives the fire times and asserts every gap is exactly 40 min rather than only pinning literals); the opt-in chain now sleeps for the pass's own elapsed time before re-dispatching, making its period two pass durations instead of one; canary hourly -> 2-hourly; canary staleness window 2h -> 4h (its own rationale is 3x cadence, which now floors at 2h). Jenkinsfile mirrors the backstop.\n\nHonest limit worth recording for whoever revisits runner contention: the pacing sleep runs inside the bridge job, so it halves chained RUNS and dispatch events but does not release the runner slot during the pause — billed wall-clock per pass is unchanged. Freeing the slot outright means turning RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS off, which is a repo Variable rather than a code change. Separately, the 609 workflow_dispatch runs in dotted-uncheery-dunnart's measurement are the Gerrit Verified lane, not the bridge; that starvation driver remains open and is untouched by this change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786621638291945001,"uuid":"e2142f34-a79f-4647-9b9f-a1108f8c2f01"}